WEBVTT

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:02.392
A timeout does not always mean nothing happened.

00:00:02.833 --> 00:00:06.397
If a real provider request may have succeeded, inspect the

00:00:06.432 --> 00:00:09.451
provider's record or a durable operation log through

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.889
authorized read-only means before retrying.

00:00:12.492 --> 00:00:15.883
If the outcome remains uncertain, report that state and

00:00:15.918 --> 00:00:17.996
the exact action needed to resolve it.

00:00:18.599 --> 00:00:21.514
An idempotency key or similar design can make repeated

00:00:21.572 --> 00:00:24.590
requests safer, but it must actually be supported and

00:00:24.648 --> 00:00:25.066
used.

00:00:25.449 --> 00:00:28.131
Do not claim an operation is safe to repeat based on a

00:00:28.178 --> 00:00:28.781
name alone.
